# CoW tier-2 L1 PROPERTY-(d) regression witness — the soundness anchor.
#
# A closure `grow` CAPTURES the source collection `v` and MUTATES it
# (`v.push`). The read-only bind `String s = v.get(0).unwrap()` comes
# AFTER the closure def, then `grow()` is INVOKED three times AFTER the
# bind, then `s` is READ.
#
# The closure-body mutation's textual span is BEFORE the bind, so a naive
# position-aware gate (max_span < bind_pos) would WRONGLY borrow-flip the
# bind even though the closure RUNS after it. Property (d) treats any
# closure-captured-mutated name as NEVER pristine (`cow_closure_mutated`),
# so the flip does NOT fire — `s` is an independent owned clone taken at the
# bind. Output correct + ASan-clean.
#
# ⚠ HONESTY (output-review NIT 2026-06-09): under the self-host's CURRENT
# by-value closure capture, `grow()` mutates a COPY — the outer `v` stays
# len 2 (see the `2` in the expected output) — so a wrong flip would NOT
# actually dangle here. This fixture therefore LOCKS IN correct output +
# Rust-parity for the closure-deferred shape, but does NOT behaviorally
# discriminate (d)-on from (d)-off at runtime. Property (d)'s code is still
# sound, load-bearing DEFENSE: required for by-reference / shared-heap
# capture and any future capture-semantics change. A stronger discriminating
# witness would need by-reference capture (not yet a language form).
#
# Expected: `s` is the snapshot of v[0] taken at the bind ("first…"); the
# three pushes do not perturb it; `v.len()` stays 2 (by-value capture).

void main():
    Vector[String] v = ["firstlonglonglonglongstring", "secondlonglonglongstring"]
    auto grow = (): v.push("grownlonglonglonglonglongstring")
    String s = v.get(0).unwrap()
    grow()
    grow()
    grow()
    print(s)
    print(s.len())
    print(v.len())
